title: Add routing
description: Add routing to your React Native application using Expo Router.
step: 5
---
In this step, you'll add some basic routing to your app.
Based on the user's login status, you'll redirect them to the login page or the home page.

## Home page {% #home-page %}

Replace the contents of `src/app/index.tsx` with the following stub code.
We'll update this page later to display the ideas posted by other users and allow the user to post their ideas.

```client-react-native
import { Button, Text, View } from "react-native";
import { useUser } from "@/contexts/UserContext";

export default function HomeScreen() {
  const user = useUser();

  return (
    <View style={{ padding: 16, gap: 16 }}>
      <Text>Welcome, {user.current?.email}</Text>
      <Button title="Logout" onPress={() => user.logout()} />
    </View>
  );
}
```

## Basic routing {% #basic-routing %}

Expo Router builds the app's navigation from the files in `src/app`.
The root layout in `src/app/_layout.tsx` wraps every screen, so it is the place to add the `UserProvider` and to decide which screens a user can open.

Each `Stack.Protected` group only allows its screens when its `guard` is `true`.
When a guard changes, Expo Router redirects the user to the first screen they are allowed to open.
Logged in users can only open the home page, and logged out users can only open the login page.

Replace the contents of `src/app/_layout.tsx` with the following code.

```client-react-native
import { Stack } from "expo-router";
import { UserProvider, useUser } from "@/contexts/UserContext";

function RootNavigator() {
  const user = useUser();

  // Wait until the current session is checked before choosing a screen.
  if (user.loading) {
    return null;
  }

  const isLoggedIn = user.current !== null;

  return (
    <Stack>
      <Stack.Protected guard={isLoggedIn}>
        <Stack.Screen name="index" options={{ title: "Home" }} />
      </Stack.Protected>
      <Stack.Protected guard={!isLoggedIn}>
        <Stack.Screen name="login" options={{ title: "Login" }} />
      </Stack.Protected>
    </Stack>
  );
}

export default function RootLayout() {
  return (
    <UserProvider>
      <RootNavigator />
    </UserProvider>
  );
}
```

## Test the routing {% #test-routing %}

Run the app using the following command.

```sh
npx expo start
```

Scan the QR code with the [Expo Go](https://expo.dev/go) app on your device, or press `a` to open the app in an Android emulator or `i` to open it in an iOS simulator.

You should see the login page.
If you create a new account, you should be logged in and redirected to the home page.
If you log out, you should be redirected back to the login page.
